+        // So is every texture an earlier encoder of the command buffer left carried that this one
+        // has not used (`ShadowCarry`): its image no longer holds the truth, so it is carried no
+        // further and copies in at its next use. DroidVM: a render encoder's copies reach no
+        // `wrote` (Metal does not order its commands), so a rotated framebuffer's pass twin copied
+        // back after a pass left the image its functions sample as an earlier encoder had it:
+        // CoreAnimation's backdrop captures of its framebuffer (a toolbar's glass while the dock
+        // rises over the app, Spotlight's field) blurred the wallpaper drawn before the app, or
+        // black, frame after frame.
+        self.carry
+            .entries
+            .retain(|carried| !carried.copies.shares_truth(&written));
